 "掴まえる": "لُقْطَة (A find, in particular a boyfriend or girlfriend or prospective spouse.) / أَمْسَكَ (to intercept an object in the air etc.) / مَسَكَ (to intercept an object in the air etc.)  [to catch]\nمثال: 警察が容疑者を捕まえた。\n→ The policeman got the suspect. / مَسَكَ (To grip suddenly; to seize; to clutch.) / قَبَضَ (To make a sudden grasping or clutching motion (at something).) / مَسْك, قَبْض (The rescue of a person from a burning structure.)  [to grab]\nمثال: その男は少年の手をつかまえた。\n→ The man took the boy by the hand. / وَقَفَ, تَوَقَّفَ (To cease moving.) / أَوْقَفَ, وَقَفَ (To cause (something) to cease moving or progressing.) / تَوَقَّفَ, وَقَّف (To cease; to no longer continue.) / أَوْقَفَ, وَقَفَ (To cause (something) to come to an end.) / مَوْقِف (A (usually marked) place where buses, trams or trains halt to let passengers get) / وَقْفَة (An action of stopping; interruption of travel.)  [to stop (e.g. a stranger in the street)]\nمثال: ここでタクシーをつかまえられますか。\n→ Can I catch a taxi here? / نَحْوَ, صَوْبَ (In the direction of.) / نَحُو (In relation to (someone or something).) / لِأَجْل (For the purpose of attaining (an aim).) / بِقُرْب (Located close to; near (a time or place).)  [towards (someone)]\nas 〜をつかまえて",
